To upgrade HL7 v2 messages from version 2.3 to 2.5 using a JavaScript step in Mirth Connect, you can use the following code:
```
// Get the current message
var msg = connectorMap.get('message');

// Check if the message is an ADT (admit/discharge/transfer) message
if (!msg.getMessageType().equals('ADT')) {
  // If not, exit this script
  return;
}

// Loop through each segment in the message
for (seg in msg.getSegments()) {
  // Get the current segment name and field number
  var segName = seg.getName();
  var fieldName = seg.getFieldNumber();

  // Check if this is an MSH (message header) segment with a Field Separator of '|'
  if (segName.equals('MSH') && !fieldName.equals(1)) {
    // If not, exit this script
    return;
  }

  // Loop through each field in the segment
  for (field in seg.getFields()) {
    // Get the current field name and value
    var fieldName = seg.getName() + '.' + field.getName();
    var fieldValue = field.getValue();

    // Check if this is an MSH-10 (date/time of transaction) field
    if (fieldName.equals('MSH.10')) {
      // If not, exit this script
      return;
    }

    // Loop through each character in the value
    for (char c in fieldValue.toCharArray()) {
      // Get the current character and name
      var charName = fieldName + '.' + c.getName();

      // Check if this is an MSH-10.1 (date/time of transaction) field with a Field Separator of '|'
      if (charName.equals('MSH.10.1') && !c.getName().equals(1)) {
        // If not, exit this script
        return;
      }

      // Replace the character with an underscore (_)
      fieldValue = fieldName + '.' + c.getName() + '_' + fieldValue.substring(c.getName().length(), fieldValue.indexOf(c.getName()) + c.getName().length());
    }
  }

  // Set the new value of the field to the original value
  seg.setField(fieldName, fieldValue);
}
```
This code loops through each segment and field in the message, checks if it's an MSH (message header) segment with a Field Separator of '|', and then upgrades any date/time fields to use underscores (_) instead of dashes (-).

