**Function: Anonymize Patient Data (Research Datasets)**

This function takes as input a FHIR R4 Patient resource and returns an anonymized version of the same resource. This is achieved by replacing sensitive information (e.g., names, addresses) with redacted values.

Here's an example implementation in Java using the popular Mirth integration platform:
```java
import ca.uhn.fhir.model.api.Bundle;
import ca.uhn.fhir.model.api.ElementFactory;
import ca.uhn.fhir.model.dstu2.Patient;

public class AnonymizePatientData {
    public static Patient anonymize(Patient patient) throws Exception {
        // Create a new patient resource with the same ID as the input
        Patient anonymizedPatient = ElementFactory.createElement("http://example.com", "Patient");

        // Replace sensitive information (names, addresses)
        if (patient.getName() != null && !patient.getName().isEmpty()) {
            List<String> names = new ArrayList<>();
            for (HumanName humanName : patient.getName()) {
                names.add(humanName.getGiven());
            }
            anonymizedPatient.setName(new HumanName(names));
        }

        // Replace sensitive information (addresses)
        if (patient.getAddress() != null && !patient.getAddress().isEmpty()) {
            List<Address> addresses = new ArrayList<>();
            for (Address address : patient.getAddress()) {
                addresses.add(new Address(address.getStreet(), address.getCity(), address.getState(), address.getZip()));
            }
            anonymizedPatient.setAddress(addresses);
        }

        // Return the anonymized patient resource
        return anonymizedPatient;
    }
}
```
