To handle this, we have three options:

1. **Ignore and continue**: We can simply ignore any ZPD segments that are not part of our expected set and continue processing the message.
2. **Error out**: We can raise an error when we encounter an unexpected Z-segment (ZPD) and stop processing the message.
3. **Validate and re-try**: We can validate the entire ADT message against a set of rules, then try again if it passes.

