To create a FHIR R4 Bundle transaction with Patient, Observation, and DiagnosticReport, we'll follow these steps:

1. Create a new FHIR client instance using your preferred programming language (e.g., Java, Python, or Node.js).
2. Define the patient's information in accordance with the US Core Must Support elements (US Core) guidelines.
3. Create an Observation resource to represent the diagnostic report and add it to our Bundle transaction.
4. Add a DiagnosticReport resource to our Bundle transaction, referencing the Observation created earlier.

Here is an example code snippet in Java using the FHIR Client library for Java (fhir-client-java):
```java
import ca.uhn.fhir.context.FhirContext;
import ca.uhn.fhir.model.api.BundleFactory;
import ca.uhn.fhir.model.dstu2.resource.Patient;
import ca.uhn.fhir.model.dstu2.resource.Observation;
import ca.uhn.fhir.model.dstu2.resource.DiagnosticReport;

// Create a new FHIR client instance
FhirContext fhirCtx = FhirContext.forR4();
BundleFactory bundleFactory = fhirCtx.newBundleFactory();

// Define the patient's information (US Core)
Patient patient = new Patient();
patient.addName(new HumanName().setGiven("John").setFamily("Doe"));
patient.setBirthDate(LocalDate.of(1990, 1, 1));
patient.addAddress(new Address().setUse(Address.Use.HOME).setLine(Arrays.asList("123 Main St")));

// Create an Observation resource (diagnostic report)
Observation observation = new Observation();
observation.setCode(new CodeableConcept().setText("Diagnostic Report"));
observation.setValue(new Quantity().setValue(10.0));

// Add the Observation to our Bundle transaction
Bundle bundle = bundleFactory.newBundle();
bundle.addEntry(new Bundle.Entry().setResource(observation));

// Create a DiagnosticReport resource and add it to our Bundle transaction
DiagnosticReport diagnosticReport = new DiagnosticReport();
diagnosticReport.setSubject(patient);
diagnosticReport.setCode(new CodeableConcept().setText("Diagnostic Report"));
diagnosticReport.setValue(new Quantity().setValue(10.0));
bundle.addEntry(new Bundle.Entry().setResource(diagnosticReport));

// Set the Bundle's type to "transaction"
bundle.setType(Bundle.Type.TRANSACTION);

// Send our Bundle transaction to the FHIR server
String fhirServerUrl = "https://example.com/fhir";
FhirClient client = new FhirClient(fhirServerUrl);
Response response = client.postBundle(bundle, 201); // create (201 Created)

if (response.getStatusCode() == 201) {
    System.out.println("Bundle transaction successful!");
} else {
    System.err.println("Error sending Bundle transaction: " + response.getBody());
}
```
