As an eHR API integration expert specializing in healthcare data interoperability, I'll provide you with a comprehensive solution for building a FHIR STU3-to-R4 migration tool for Patient resources.

**Tool Name:** `stufhir-migration-tool`

**Language:** Java (with the popular Apache Maven build tool)

**Purpose:**
Create a new patient resource in R4 format from an existing patient resource in STU3 format, handling changes to the following elements:

* identifier (XPN-5)
* name (XPN-1, XPN-2)
* birthDate (XPN-7)
* gender (XPN-8)

**Code Example:**
```java
import ca.uhn.fhir.model.api.Bundle;
import ca.uhn.fhir.model.api.ElementFactory;
import ca.uhn.fhir.rest.client.api.IGenericClient;

public class StufhirMigrationTool {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        // Load the STU3 patient resource from a file or database
        Bundle stu3Patient = loadStu3Patient("path/to/stu3_patient.json");

        // Create an empty R4 Patient resource
        Bundle r4Patient = new Bundle();
        r4Patient.setType(Bundle.TYPE_PATIENT);

        try {
            // Iterate through the STU3 patient's identifiers (XPN-5)
            for (Bundle.BundleEntryComponent entry : stu3Patient.getEntry()) {
                if (entry.getComponent().get(0).getCode().equals("XPN-5")) {
                    // Create a new R4 Patient identifier
                    r4Patient.addIdentifier(new Identifier()
                            .setSystem(entry.getComponent().get(1).getValue())
                            .setValue(entry.getComponent().get(2).getValue()));

                    // Iterate through the STU3 patient's names (XPN-1, XPN-2)
                    for (Bundle.BundleEntryComponent entry : stu3Patient.getEntry()) {
                        if (entry.getComponent().get(0).getCode().equals("XPN-1") ||
                                entry.getComponent().get(0).getCode().equals("XPN-2")) {

                            // Create a new R4 Patient name
                            r4Patient.addName(new HumanName()
                                    .setUse(HumanName.Use.OFFICIAL)
                                    .addGiven(entry.getComponent().get(1).getValue())
                                    .addFamily(entry.getComponent().get(2).getValue()));

                        }
                    }

                    // Iterate through the STU3 patient's birth date (XPN-7)
                    for (Bundle.BundleEntryComponent entry : stu3Patient.getEntry()) {
                        if (entry.getComponent().get(0).getCode().equals("XPN-7")) {

                            // Create a new R4 Patient birth date
                            r4Patient.addBirthDate(new DateTimeType(entry.getComponent().getValue()));

                        }
                    }

                    // Iterate through the STU3 patient's gender (XPN-8)
                    for (Bundle.BundleEntryComponent entry : stu3Patient.getEntry()) {
                        if (entry.getComponent().get(0).getCode().equals("XPN-8")) {

                            // Create a new R4 Patient gender
                            r4Patient.addGender(new CodeableConcept()
                                    .setText(entry.getComponent().getValue())
                                    .addCoding(new Coding()
                                            .setSystem("http://terminology.org/iso/3166/all")
                                            .setCode(entry.getComponent().get(1).getValue())));

                        }
                    }

                }
            }

        } catch (Exception e) {
            System.out.println("Error: " + e.getMessage());
            return;
        }

        // Create a new R4 Patient resource
        IGenericClient client = ClientFactory.create();
        Patient r4PatientResource = client.createPatient(r4Patient);

        // Print the converted R4 patient resource to the console (or log file)
        System.out.println(new JSONObject(r4PatientResource).toString());
    }
}
```
**Error Handling:**

* Catch any exceptions that may occur during the migration process and print an error message with a human-readable format (`"Error: " + e.getMessage()`)
* In case of an error, simply return from the code (i.e., exit)

**Code Organization:**
The Stufhir Migration Tool will consist of three main components:

1.  **STU3-to-R4 converter**: This component will iterate through the STU3 patient's identifiers, names, birth date, and gender elements, creating a new R4 Patient resource with updated values.
2.  **FHIR client**: This component will use the popular Apache FHIR Client library (Apache FHIR Client) to create an empty R4 Patient resource using the `IGenericClient` interface.

