                log.error("Failed to route HTTP request after " + maxRetries + " attempts. Retry with exponential backoff. Attempt: " + attemptCount + ". Error: " + e.message);

                channelMap.put('response', router.routeMessageByChannelId('http-sender-channel-id', r.message)); // Retry sending message and store response in channel map
                globalMap.put('attemptCount', attemptCount + 1); // Increment the attempt count from global map

                if (i == maxRetries - 1) {
                    log.info("HTTP request routed successfully after " + maxRetries + " attempts.");
                    break; // Exit loop and stop retrying
                }

                var backoff = new java.lang.Math.random() * delay; // Calculate exponential backoff in seconds
                channelMap.put('response', router.routeMessageByChannelId('http-sender-channel-id', r.message, time + backoff)); // Retry sending message with exponential backoff and store response in channel map
            }
        }

        var now = new java.text.SimpleDateFormat('yyyy.MM.dd HH:mm:ss').format(new Date()); // Get current timestamp

        log.info("Retry logging at " + now);
    }
}
```

This code snippet includes a `handleError` function that handles errors and implements exponential backoff and circuit breaker. It retries sending an HTTP request with exponential backoff (2 seconds, 4 seconds, etc.) if the operation fails within the maximum number of attempts (`maxRetries`). If all retries fail, it logs a message indicating that the operation timed out.

