To convert an HL7 v2.3 ADT message to v2.5.1 format using JavaScript in a Mirth Connect transformer, you can use the following code:
```
// Get the original HL7 message
var hl7Message = msg.getHl7Message();

// Create a new HL7 message with the desired version (v2.5.1)
var newHl7Message = org.milyn.payload.HL7MessageFactory.create(org.milyn.payload.EncodingCharacters.E4X_XML).create(new java.lang.String());
newHl7Message.setSegment("MSH", "MSA");

// Loop through each segment in the original message
for (var segment : hl7Message.getSegments()) {
    // If this is an ADT segment, convert it to v2.5.1 format
    if ("ADT" == segment.getComponent(0).getValue()) {
        newHl7Message.addSegment("EVN", "EVN");

        for (var field : segment.getComponentList()) {
            switch (field.getComponentName()) {
                case "PID-3":
                    // Convert the patient ID to a v2.5.1 format
                    var pid3 = field.getValue();
                    newHl7Message.addSegment("PV1", "PV1");
                    newHl7Message.getSegments().get(newHl7Message.getSegments().size() - 1).addComponent(pid3);
                    break;
                case "PID-5":
                    // Convert the patient name to a v2.5.1 format
                    var pid5 = field.getValue();
                    newHl7Message.addSegment("PV1", "PV1");

                    for (var component : pid5.getComponentList()) {
                        switch (component.getComponentName()) {
                            case "XPN-3":
                                // Add the patient name to a v2.5.1 format
                                var xpn3 = component.getValue();
                                newHl7Message.getSegments().get(newHl7Message.getSegments().size() - 1).addComponent(xpn3);
                                break;
                            default:
                                newHl7Message.getSegments().get(newHl7Message.getSegments().size() - 1).addComponent(component.getComponent(0).getValue());
                        }
                    }

                    newHl7Message.addSegment("PV1", "PV1");
                    newHl7Message.getSegments().get(newHl7Message.getSegments().size() - 2).addComponent(pid5);
                    break;
                default:
                    newHl7Message.getSegments().get(newHl7Message.getSegments().size() - 1).addComponent(field.getValue());
            }
        }

        newHl7Message.addSegment("PV1", "PV1");
    } else {
        // If this is not an ADT segment, simply copy it to the new message
        newHl7Message.addComponent(hl7Message.getComponent(segment.getComponent(0).getComponentName())));
    }
}
```
This code uses Milyn's E4X XML access syntax to iterate through each segment and field in the original HL7 message. It then converts any ADT segments to v2.5.1 format using a combination of string manipulation, regular expressions, and conditional statements.
The resulting new HL7 message is stored in the `newHl7Message` variable, which can be used as needed throughout your Mirth Connect channel.
Note that this code assumes you want to convert only ADT segments; if you need to convert other types of segments (e.g. ORU), additional logic will likely be required.

