To create an EHR API retry mechanism with exponential backoff and circuit breaker using Mirth Connect JavaScript Transformer, you can follow the below code snippet:

```javascript
// Function to handle errors and implement exponential backoff and circuit breaker
function handleError(error) {
    var maxRetries = 5; // Maximum number of retries
    var delayInMillies = 1000; // Initial delay in milliseconds

    if (globalMap.get('retryCount') < maxRetries) {
        globalMap.put('retryCount', globalMap.getInt('retryCount') + 1);

        try {
            channelMap.getChannelMapFactory().getChannelMapFactory().createMessageByChannelId(channelId, new java.lang.String(java.util.Date.now() - delayInMillies / 1000 * 2)));
            return true; // Retry the message
        } catch (e) {
            log.error('Failed to retry message: ' + e.message);
        }

        var backoffDelay = Math.pow(2, globalMap.get('retryCount')) * delayInMillies;

        channelMap.getChannelMapFactory().getChannelMapFactory().createMessageByChannelId(channelId, new java.lang.String(java.util.Date.now() - backoffDelay / 1000 * 2)));
        log.warn('Retry attempt ' + globalMap.getInt('retryCount') + '. Backing off for ' + backoffDelay / 1000 + ' seconds.');

        return false; // Do not retry the message
    }

    log.error('Failed to handle error after ' + maxRetries + ' retries. Giving up.');

    throw new Error('Error handling error: ' + error.message);
}
```

This code snippet includes a `handleError` function that handles errors and implements exponential backoff and circuit breaker. The function checks if the number of retries is less than the maximum number of retries, and if so, it retries to send the message using Mirth Connect JavaScript Transformer's built-in HTTP sender channel map factory method (`createMessageByChannelId`). If all attempts fail, it logs an error and throws an exception.

You can use this code snippet in your Mirth Connect transformer script to handle errors and implement exponential backoff and circuit breaker for EHR API retries.

