To create a Mirth deployment script that exports channel configuration as an E4X XML file, we'll follow these steps:

1. Get the `channelId` and `exportFile` variables from the current thread
2. Create an empty XML file using the `<java.io.FileWriter>` class
3. Use the `E4X XML Builder` to create a new `<channel-config>` node with the desired attributes (e.g., `id`, `name`, etc.)
4. Loop through each child node of the `<channel-config>` node and recursively export its configuration as an E4X XML file using the same steps 2-3 above
5. Write the exported channel configurations to the original XML file

Here's our Mirth deployment script:
```javascript
// Get the channelId and exportFile variables from the current thread
var channelId = getChannelId();
var exportFile = new java.io.FileWriter('/path/to/export/config.xml');

// Create an empty XML file using the <java.io.FileWriter> class
exportFile.write('<channel-configs>');

try {
  // Loop through each child node of the <channel-config> node and recursively export its configuration as an E4X XML file
  for (var config in getChannelConfigs(channelId)) {
    var configXml = new java.lang.StringBuilder();
    configXml.append('<' + channelId + '-config>');

    for (var childConfig in config.getChildNodes()) {
      if (!childConfig.hasSimpleContent()) continue;

      // Recursively export its configuration as an E4X XML file
      var childConfigXml = getExportChildConfig(childConfig, configXml.toString());
      configXml.append(childConfigXml);
    }

    // Write the exported channel configurations to the original XML file
    exportFile.write(configXml.toString() + '</' + channelId + '-config>');
} finally {
  // Close the XML writer
  exportFile.close();
}

// Helper function: Recursively exports a child node's configuration as an E4X XML file
function getExportChildConfig(childNode, parentXml) {
  var childConfigXml = new java.lang.StringBuilder(parentXml + '/' + childNode.getName());

  // Loop through each child node of the <child-node> node and recursively export its configuration as an E4X XML file
  for (var grandchild in getNode(childNode).getChildNodes()) {
    if (!grandchild.hasSimpleContent()) continue;

    // Recursively export its configuration as an E4X XML file
    var grandchildConfigXml = getExportGrandchildConfig(grandchild, childConfigXml.toString());
    childConfigXml.append(grandchildConfigXml);
  }

  return new java.lang.StringBuilder(childConfigXml + '.xml');
}
```
Note that this script assumes you have the `getChannelId()` and `getNode()` functions available to retrieve the current channel ID and node hierarchy, respectively.

