1. Register an app at App Orchard (open.epic.com) to obtain a client ID and secret.
2. Generate an RSA key pair and upload the public key to Epic's API management platform.
3. Create a signed JWT assertion using the private key and client credentials.
4. Exchange the JWT for an access token by sending a POST request to the token endpoint (https://fhir.epic.com/interconnect-fhir-oauth/api/FHIR/R4/oauth2/token) with the following parameters:

* grant_type=client_credentials
* &client_assertion_type=urn:ietf:params:oauth:client-assertion-type:jwt-bearer
* &client_assertion={signed_jwt}

5. Use the access token to make API calls, including sending a GET request (https://fhir.epic.com/interconnect-fhir-oauth/api/FHIR/R4/Patient/$export) with an Accept header set to application/fhir+json and Prefer header set to respond-async.

