1. Get the `channelId` and `exportFile` variables from the current thread
2. Create an empty XML file using the `<java.io.FileWriter>` class
3. Use the `E4X XML Builder` to create a new `<channelConfig>` node with the desired attributes (e.g., `id`, `name`, etc.)
4. Loop through each child node (`<rec`) of the channel configuration and recursively export its contents as an E4X XML file using the same script

Here's the final code:
```javascript
// Get the channelId and exportFile variables from the current thread
var channelId = getChannelId();
var exportFile = new java.io.FileWriter('/path/to/export/' + channelId + '.xml');

try {
  // Create an empty XML file using the <java.io.FileWriter> class
  var xmlBuilder = e4x.E4XXMLBuilder();

  // Get the channel configuration as a JavaScript object (e.g., `channelMap`)
  var channelConfig = getChannelMap().get(channelId);

  // Use E4X to create a new <channelConfig> node with desired attributes
  var channelConfigNode = xmlBuilder.createElement('channelConfig');
  channelConfigNode.setAttribute('id', channelId);
  channelConfigNode.setAttribute('name', channelConfig.getName());

  // Loop through each child node (`<rec`) of the channel configuration and recursively export its contents as an E4X XML file
  for (var rec in getChannelMap().get(channelId).getReps()) {
    var recNode = xmlBuilder.createElement(rec.getName());
    recNode.setAttribute('name', rec.getName());

    // Recursively export the child node's contents as an E4X XML file using the same script
    try {
      exportFile.write(recNode.toString() + '\n');
      for (var childRec in getChannelMap().get(channelId).getReps()) {
        if (!rec.getName().equals(childRec.getName())) {
          exportFile.write(childRecNode.toString() + '\n');
        }
      }
    } catch (e) {}

  }

  // Write the channel configuration to the XML file
  exportFile.write(channelConfigNode.toString());

} finally {
  // Close the XML file writer
  exportFile.close();
}
```
