The issue you're experiencing is known as "half-open" behavior! When a client (in this case, your Mirth channel) sends an HL7 message and doesn't receive any response from the server (in this case, the EHR system), it will wait for a certain amount of time before giving up.

To fix this issue, let's add some retry logic with exponential backoff to our Mirth channel. We can use Java's built-in `java.net.Socket` class to achieve this. Here's an example code snippet:
```
import java.io.Closeable;
import java.io.IOException;
import java.util.concurrent.TimeUnit;

// ... (rest of the code remains the same)

// Set a maximum number of retries and a delay between each attempt
int maxRetries = 5;
long retryDelayMs = 1000; // 1 second

for (int i = 0; i <= maxRetries; i++) {
    try {
        // Create a new socket connection to the EHR system
        Closeable socket = java.net.Socket.create();

        // Send our HL7 message and wait for an ACK response
        java.io.OutputStream out = socket.getOutputStream();
        out.write(hl7Message.getBytes());
        out.close();

        java.nio.ByteBuffer in = java.nio.ByteBuffer.allocate(1024);
        int ackResponse = -1;
        while ((in.get() & 0xFF) != '\r') {
            // Read the ACK response from the EHR system
            ackResponse = in.getInt();
        }

        if (ackResponse == HL7.ACK_OK) { // Got an ACK! We're good to go!
            break;
        } else {
            throw new Exception("EHR system returned a non-ACK: " + java.lang.Integer.toHexString(ackResponse));
        }
    } catch (IOException e) {
        System.out.println("Error sending HL7 message: " + e.getMessage());

        // Wait for a short period before retrying
        TimeUnit.MILLISECONDS.sleep(retryDelayMs);

        if (i < maxRetries) { // We're still within our maximum number of retries, so let's try again!
            continue;
        } else {
            throw new Exception("Failed to receive an ACK from EHR system after " + maxRetries + " attempts");
        }
    }
}
```

