To upgrade HL7 v2 messages from version 2.3 to 2.5 using Mirth Connect JavaScript Transformer, you can use the following code:
```
// Get the original message
var msg = router.getMessage();

// Check if the message is an ADT (Admission/Discharge Transfer) message
if (!msg.getMSH().getSegment("EVN").getValue()) {
  // If not, exit this transformer
  return;
}

// Loop through each segment in the original message
for (var seg : msg.getSegments()) {
  // Check if the segment is an MSH (Message Header) segment
  if (!seg.getComponent(1).toString().equals("MSH")) {
    // If not, exit this transformer
    return;
  }

  // Loop through each field in the original message
  for (var fld : seg.getFields()) {
    // Check if the field is an MSH-3 (Sending Application) field
    if (!fld.getComponent(1).toString().equals("MSH-3")) {
      // If not, exit this transformer
      return;
    }

    // Loop through each component in the original message
    for (var cmp : fld.getComponents()) {
      // Check if the component is an MSH-3.1 (Sending Application Name) field
      if (!cmp.getComponent(1).toString().equals("MSH-3.1")) {
        // If not, exit this transformer
        return;
      }

      // Upgrade the original message to version 2.5
      msg.getSegments()[0].getFields()[0].getComponents()[0] = cmp.getComponent(1) + " - Version 2.5";
    }
  }
}
```
This code loops through each segment and field in the original message, checks if it's an MSH-3 (Sending Application) field, and upgrades its value to version 2.5 using a simple string concatenation operation.

